  BSA_ref notes ```
Body surface area of the reference individual of the age, Du Bois formula; the reference
of the skin.

`BSA_ref = 0.007184 m2 * (BW_ref / 1 kg)^0.425 * (HEIGHT_ref / 1 cm)^0.725` 

Sources:

- Du Bois D, Du Bois EF. Clinical calorimetry, tenth paper: a formula to estimate the approximate surface area if height and weight be known. Arch Intern Med 17(6_2):863-871, 1916. doi:10.1001/archinte.1916.00080130010002
```
  fage_FFM notes ```
1 at 35 years, the age of the individual of a build without the physiology over age
(`PBPKDefinition.age`, which gives the curve of `pkpdsim.pbpk.age`): the multiplier of the Janmahasatian 2005 fat-free
mass of boys, 0.88 + (1 - 0.88)/(1 + (AGE/13.4)^-12.7); model M2 of Al-Sallami 2015
Table 4, read from the paper: a = 0.88 (bootstrap 95 % CI 0.87-0.89), the sigmoidicity
c = 12.7 (13.0, 5.2-19.0) and the maturation half time A50 = 13.4 years (13.4, 12.7-13.8),
with the upper bound b fixed to 1 so that the asymptote is the adult model. The index
dataset is 853 dual energy X-ray absorptiometry measurements of 515 males of a median
age of 13.8 years (range 3-29.7) and a median body mass index of 19.9 kg/m2 (13.6-36.2),
the external test dataset 86 males. Relative to 20 years, 1 from 20 years; extrapolated
below 3 years. Against the reference children of Fomon 1982 Table I (chemical analysis
and balance data) the chain of Janmahasatian 2005 and this factor gives 0.97 to 0.92
of their fat-free mass over 3 to 10 years, so it under-predicts the fat-free mass
of a child by 3 to 8 % and puts its body fat at 18 to 20 % against their 13 to 18
%.

Sources:

- Al-Sallami HS, Goulding A, Grant A, Taylor R, Holford N, Duffull SB. Prediction of fat-free mass in children. Clin Pharmacokinet 54(11):1169-1178, 2015. doi:10.1007/s40262-015-0277-z
- Fomon SJ, Haschke F, Ziegler EE, Nelson SE. Body composition of reference children from birth to age 10 years. Am J Clin Nutr 35(5):1169-1175, 1982. doi:10.1093/ajcn/35.5.1169
```
  FFM_ref notes ```
Fat-free mass of the reference individual of the age, the male formula of Janmahasatian
2005 times the factor of the children (Al-Sallami 2015).

`FFM_ref = BW_ref * 9270 dimensionless / (6680 dimensionless + 216 dimensionless * (BW_ref / 1 kg) / (HEIGHT_ref / 100 cm)^2) * fage_FFM` 

Sources:

- Janmahasatian S, Duffull SB, Ash S, Ward LC, Byrne NM, Green B. Quantification of lean bodyweight. Clin Pharmacokinet 44(10):1051-1065, 2005. doi:10.2165/00003088-200544100-00004
- Al-Sallami HS, Goulding A, Grant A, Taylor R, Holford N, Duffull SB. Prediction of fat-free mass in children. Clin Pharmacokinet 54(11):1169-1178, 2015. doi:10.1007/s40262-015-0277-z
```
